cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "calibaudit: Brier decomposition, calibration-error bias and held-out recalibration audit for binary probabilistic forecasts"
abstract: >-
  Murphy decomposition of the Brier score with an exact five-term identity that
  holds for any binning, bootstrap reliability diagrams with measured coverage,
  the expected calibration error with its binning bias quantified against
  forecasts of known calibration, and a held-out audit of Platt scaling and
  isotonic regression against the raw forecast as baseline, reporting the
  sample sizes at which recalibration makes the score worse. Research-grade;
  not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational aerospace
  use.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
license: Apache-2.0
